  "name": "Sovol SV08 stock toolhead (planetary extruder, 5020 front blower, rear 3010 duct, inductive probe)",
  "provenance": "Sovol SV08 stock toolhead (planetary extruder, 5020 front blower, rear 3010 duct, inductive probe) Confidence: high. Sources: https://github.com/Sovol3d/SV08/tree/main/STEP (0JXHSV08-00000 Frame 3d printer pre-assembled.zip, JXHSV08-06000 hotend assembly planetary.step). Full-printer STEP is Y-up with +Z toward the front (screen side); mapped to printer frame X=x, Y=-z, Z=y. Tip = lowest point of the nozzle part (NAUO127, 49.5 mm long nozzle with integrated heatbreak), axis = centre of the tip face. Lowest non-nozzle parts: extruder install plate (z 1.82, x -27.3..-12.2, y 17.8..25.7), extruder cover 5020 / front shroud lips (z 1.90, two clusters x -27.3..-10.7 and 8.7..25.6), inductive probe (z 1.90, x -22.8..-10.8, y 4.2..17.2). The front shroud rises toward the front (y down to -36.7 only from z ~2.5). Rear 3010 air deflector (z 2.88) reaches back to y 59 under the gantry; silicone sock starts at z 6.0, ceramic heater at 8.8. Probe height is as modelled by Sovol (1.9 mm above tip); users may set it differently. Bed and frame parts excluded. Nozzle: land radius 0.41 mm, 36.2-degree cone to Z=3.50, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 37.40 mm above the tip, Y 17.9..60.7, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/sovol-sv08.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
